title: WombKeeperStart
---
<<if !has_npc_been_contacted("WombKeeper")>>
    Womb Keeper: Good, you're awake. You're lucky to be alive, child.
    -> This isn't real, is it? I've been dreaming... but this feels different.
        <<make_contact_with_npc "WombKeeper">>
        <<jump WombKeeperDialogue01>>
<<else>>
   <<jump WombKeeperStartAgain>> 
<<endif>>
===

title: WombKeeperStartAgain
---
Womb Keeper: I touch your presence. What purpose may I serve?
-> I had a question.
    <<jump WombKeeperDialogue01A_QA>>
-> Uh, nope.. I'm was just leaving.


===

title: WombKeeperDialogue01
---
Womb Keeper: Not a dream. I release you from dreams.
-> But I'm conversing with you without speaking. And I don't remember how I got here.
Womb Keeper: You have been modified. This explains how we're speaking and why you forget how you got here.
-> Modified? How?
    <<jump WombKeeperDialogue01A>>
-> All right, I will be leaving.
===

title: WombKeeperDialogue01A
---
Womb Keeper: You have been improved. I oversaw the process. We can now inform you of the essentials. You may report to ones such as I.
Womb Keeper: You were dissarrayed when you were abandoned to my care. I tended your womb and enacted the appropriate changes. That is all I will say. The rest you would not understand.
===

title: WombKeeperDialogue01A_QA
---
-> How was I improved?
    <<jump WombKeeperDialogue03A>>
-> You mentioned you oversaw my recovery. Was someone else here?
    <<jump WombKeeperDialogue03B>>
-> [Leave]
===

title: WombKeeperDialogue02A
---
Womb Keeper: What does a newborn animal remember? Something of the nothingness before? I think not.
-> I'm not a newborn. I remember fragments. Tell me something. What is this place?
    <<jump WombKeeperDialogue02B>>
-> I'm not a newborn. I should be leaving.
===

title: WombKeeperDialogue02B
---
Womb Keeper: This is a womb. You were left here when you died. I delivered you when the time was right.
-> Who left me here? 
    Womb Keeper: A sister of the kin. Them that move about these halls. Sheolites, you call them, or so I am told.
    -> An alien? They brought you my dead body?
        Womb Keeper: Yes. Dead. And not. We two of the kin disagree on the definition.
        -> I better get going.
        -> The kin... I almost... Oughh... my head hurts.
-> I was dead?
    Womb Keeper: Broken. Components disordered. One does not cheat death. Reborn. Your life starts here.
    -> Ok, well, I appreciate any aid. If you really saved my life, I guess I should be grateful.
    Womb Keeper: No need.
===

title: WombKeeperDialogue02C
---
Womb Keeper: Yet I knew so little of how your kind is organized on the inside.
Womb Keeper: You'll have to forgive me if things are arranged quite differently than you remember.
Womb Keeper: Have no fear, you will continue on in this form, as have all my womb-children.
===

title: WombKeeperDialogue03A
---
Womb Keeper: New components in, old ones out. Toward perfection... improved. Old memories, reshuffled, but not gone.
Womb Keeper: New Input and Output shunts. Makes vibrating air with human voice obsolete. You'll see.
<<jump WombKeeperDialogue01A_QA>>
===
title: WombKeeperDialogue03B
---
Womb Keeper: Thralls, yes. And the kin which entrusted you to me.
<<jump WombKeeperDialogue03B_QA>>
===
title: WombKeeperDialogue03B_QA
---
-> Where are these thralls now?
    Womb Keeper: Not needed. Served their purpose. Back to mines, most of them.
-> What are you going to do with me?
    Womb Keeper: You must leave. You may not become a thrall. The Kindred was clear on this.
-> Goodbye.
===